        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: راسته",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "راسته (râste) — \"a row (of the bazaar given to one trade)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در راسته فرش فروشها قدم زدیم. Dar râste-ye farsh-forush-hâ qadam zadim. We walked along the carpet sellers' row."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Each râste of an old bazaar belongs to one trade: gold, copper, cloth, spices."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "râste is a native word, which EtymDB lists; it is built on râst 'straight', usually traced to Middle Persian rāst: a straight line of shops."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
