          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کاروانسرا (kârvânsarâ) — \"a caravanserai, a roadside inn for caravans\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسافران قدیم شب را در کاروانسرا میگذراندند. Mosâferân-e qadim shab râ dar kârvânsarâ migozarândand. Travellers in the old days spent the night in a caravanserai."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kârvân 'caravan' + sarâ 'house'. English caravanserai comes from the Persian word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kârvânsarâ is a native compound of kârvân 'caravan', which EtymDB traces to Middle Persian kārawān 'caravan; an army on the march', and sarâ 'house, palace'. EtymDB gives the Persian word as the source of English caravanserai."
            }
          ]
